# Binary-distribution CDN hostnames only. Never service or account hostnames:
# a service domain resolved direct while its app runs through the proxy puts the
# same account in two countries at once. CDN hostnames carry no account identity.
#
# Listed below: vendor-operated CDNs that serve Russia normally. Not yet verified
# by a real transfer, so a failure here shows up as a download that stalls after
# roughly 16 KB rather than as an error. The fix is to move the hostname into
# sources/override-proxy, rebuild, and it returns to the cascade.
#
# See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-09-bulk-cdn-hosts.md for the candidates
# deliberately held back — the Akamai-fronted ones, whose address space is itself
# partly restricted in Russia.

# Steam. Also wins back the ISP-local Steam caches, which the tunnel hides:
# through the proxy these downloads come from Finland instead.
steamcontent.com
steamstatic.com
# Akamai-fronted. Added because cdn.akamai.steamstatic.com — same CDN, same
# path — pulled 50 MB at 102 Mbit/s direct. Still owed a direct measurement.
steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net

# Google binaries — Play packages, Chrome, toolchains.
dl.google.com
gvt1.com
gvt2.com

# Windows Update and Delivery Optimization.
download.windowsupdate.com
dl.delivery.mp.microsoft.com
tlu.dl.delivery.mp.microsoft.com

# Apple system and app updates.
swcdn.apple.com
swdist.apple.com
updates-http.cdn-apple.com
